# Pitiless Carnage sacrificing one merged creature (Cubwarden mutated onto Ornithopter) draws one card, not two: "that
# many" is the permanents sacrificed (CR 730.2), not the cards the merged one becomes (CR 730.3c). Cubwarden mutates on
# turn three; on turn five Bot1's hand is Pitiless Carnage and an Island when it is cast, so the one card drawn leaves two.
[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Cubwarden
Pitiless Carnage
Swamp
Island x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cubwarden.Cast(Ornithopter; Ability: Mutate)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
? Bot1.Hand = Island; Pitiless Carnage
Bot1.Hand.Pitiless Carnage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Cubwarden)
Bot1.Pass
[Expect]
